@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+# Payline — Send USDC on Ethereum
+
+A single-purpose payment page: connect a wallet, enter an ENS name or address,
+send USDC. Balances (USDC and ETH), the USD value of everything on screen, and
+the estimated gas cost are shown before you sign. Non-custodial — the app never
+touches funds.
+
+- **Chain:** Ethereum mainnet (`/src/lib/chain.ts`)
+- **Token:** USDC `0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48`, 6 decimals
+- **Page:** `/pay` (`/` redirects there)
+
+## Stack
+
+Next.js (App Router) · wagmi + viem · RainbowKit · TanStack Query · Tailwind v4.
+
+## Setup
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # fill in the values below
+npm run dev
+```
+
+| Variable | Required | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL` | production | Dedicated mainnet RPC. Without it viem falls back to a shared public node that will rate-limit real traffic. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | production | WalletConnect/Reown id from [cloud.reown.com](https://cloud.reown.com). Without it only injected browser wallets can connect. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` | production | Canonical origin for OG/Twitter card URLs. |
+
+```bash
+npm run build      # production build (runs typecheck)
+npm run typecheck
+npm run lint
+```
+
+## How it behaves
+
+**Recipient.** Accepts an ENS name or a hex address. Names are resolved onchain
+and the resolved address is displayed (and linked to Etherscan) before you can
+submit; that resolved address is what gets sent. Every rejection states its
+reason instead of silently disabling the button. Sending to the USDC contract
+itself is blocked, and sending to your own address is flagged.
+
+**Amounts.** Parsed and rendered in USDC's real 6 decimals via
+`parseUnits`/`formatUnits`. Base units are never displayed. More than 6 decimal
+places is rejected rather than truncated.
+
+**Prices.** USD figures come from Chainlink's mainnet ETH/USD and USDC/USD
+aggregators — same RPC as everything else, no extra API key. If a feed is past
+twice its heartbeat the value is labelled `stale price`; if it can't be read at
+all, the app says the USD value is unavailable rather than hiding it.
+
+**Gas.** The transfer is gas-estimated against the real call before the wallet
+opens, so reverts (insufficient balance, blocklisted address) surface early. The
+estimated fee is shown in ETH and USD, and a low ETH balance gets an explicit
+warning.
+
+**Transaction flow.** One primary button, one step at a time: connect → switch
+to Ethereum → send. The pending state is held from click through the receipt
+*and* the balance refetch, and released in `finally`, so a rejected signature
+can't lock the button. Wallet and revert errors are translated to plain language
+(`src/lib/errors.ts`) and shown next to the action.
+
+**Theming.** Semantic tokens in `globals.css` with light and dark variants that
+follow the OS; RainbowKit's modal follows the same scheme. No theme toggle, so
+there is nothing to fall out of sync.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+src/app/pay/page.tsx      the page
+src/components/PayForm    form, gas estimate, send flow, primary action
+src/lib/chain.ts          target chain + RPC (change the chain here)
+src/lib/token.ts          USDC address and decimals
+src/lib/prices.ts         Chainlink feeds + staleness
+src/lib/useRecipient.ts   ENS resolution and input validation
+src/lib/errors.ts         wallet/revert errors → human text
+```
+
+## Note on `next.config.ts`
+
+RainbowKit statically pulls in the Base Account connector, which reaches
+`@coinbase/cdp-sdk` and its optional `@x402/*` peers. Payline never uses that
+path, so those specifiers are aliased to a stub module rather than installing
+four unused packages. Revisit when RainbowKit stops importing it eagerly.
